The interface maps a key to a shard index; the router uses whichever strategy is configured.
```csharp
public interface IShardKeyStrategy {
    int GetShard(string key, int shardCount);
}
public class HashShardStrategy : IShardKeyStrategy {
    public int GetShard(string key, int shardCount) {
        uint h = 2166136261;
        foreach (char c in key) h = (h ^ c) * 16777619;
        return (int)(h % (uint)shardCount);
    }
}
```
A RangeShardStrategy would look up the key in a sorted list of range boundaries. Note string.GetHashCode is randomised per process, so use a stable hash.

